day_03_hotel
[background arg="res://assets/backgrounds/hotel_placeholder.jpg" fade="0.0"]
Narrator: A row of stalls lines the main road. Arlette is there, off duty, haggling cheerfully with a fruit seller.
join Arlette center
Arlette: You seem to really get your foothold in this town. 3 days already, most people would have left by now.
catherine: I don’t  really have a choice if I wanna live.
Arlette: You know there are many doctors in other towns, towns that are more welcoming and less.. weird than this one.
catherine: I know that none of them have provided a cure for me. If there was someone capable of that, I would've known it by now..
catherine: And if you think this town is that bad, why don’t you leave yourself ?
Arlette: I’ve got my own issues and things that make me stay in this town.
- Dig up Arlette's story
	catherine: What do you mean, you too are looking for someone ?
	Arlette: Well, yes actually. But meeting “that” someone is a bit complicated.
	catherine: So what is it ?
	Arlette: Have you even been told to mind your own business ?
	catherine: You listened to my story and I stayed at your inn. Of course listening to you is the least I can do.
	Arlette: That's really kind of you, I thought you were just someone obsessed with your own… quest.
	Arlette: well, I.. you might have seen it but this doesn't have many people yet I am still taking care of it.
	catherine: Yes, I was even wondering if it’s sustainable
	Arlette: Well .. no, of course not. This town is pretty much dead. But I have been tasked to look over this inn in exchange for my parents ?
	catherine: Your parents ? I’ve never met them.
	Arlette: They are not really here. Actually, I … what I do is my dream job right now. But I had to sacrifice something or someone in order to get it. And that someone is.. my parents
	Arlette: I know it’s stupid and greedy. People you care about for an inn.. but I’ve been fooled. And my only way to gain them back is to keep this inn running
	catherine: That sounds awful.
	Arlette: Well it is, but it’s also the reason this inn won’t close even if I run out of money.
	Arlette: So, I need to meet that monster who fooled me and try to get what I lost with any means possible.
	catherine: I see, we are in the same boat.
	Arlette: haha, well.. you should keep going, you have to find what or who you are searching for.
	set {ChapterTracking.is_evil} = true
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} -= 1.0
- Cheer Arlette up saying this town ain’t that bad
	catherine: I am sorry if you didn’t want to bring that up.
	Arlette: No, it’s fine. It’s fine.
	Arlette: well .. hum.. I hope you find out what you are after. I don’t think the creatures are as villainous as this town makes them out to be.
	catherine: Yes.. Thank you. I am going to go now.
	set {ChapterTracking.is_evil} = false
	set {EndingTracking.catherine_sympathy} += 1.0
jump day_03_monster/